schema: "0.4"
id: cockpit-10-learning-plan-dashboard
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns — a terminal-native personal knowledge base (CLI, no web UI) — Learning Plan Dashboard.
# HERO screen (overlap: cockpit vs scholar side-by-side) — must read unmistakably as Cockpit.
# Theme tenets (Cockpit): cool graphite panes divided by box-drawing rules, ONE electric-magenta signal for
#   selection/focus, disciplined four-color status set, mono data + tight grotesk labels, radius 0-1px, flat (no shadows).
# Palette (do NOT write these hex into prompt.text): canvas #0e1116, ink #c9d1d9, active-pane #161b22,
#   dim border #30363d, magenta accent #ff2e88; status green #3fb950 / amber #d29922 / red #f85149 / blue #58a6ff.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity mockup of a dense TERMINAL user
    interface (TUI) — a modern "mission control" dashboard in the lineage of k9s, btop, and lazygit.
    This is rendered INSIDE a terminal window: no browser chrome, no marketing whitespace, no rounded
    cards, no drop shadows. Cool blue-graphite panes are divided by thin box-drawing rules; a SINGLE
    electric-magenta signal marks the active pane and the selected element; status uses a rationed
    four-color set (signal green, amber, red, blue), each paired with a glyph; meters and sparklines
    are drawn with block glyphs (▁▂▃▄▅▆▇█ and █████░░). Monospaced type for all data, values and
    meters; a tight grotesk for pane titles and labels only. Every pixel is instrumentation. This is
    the densest, most instrument-like screen of the product — a packed grid of live gauges.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity screenshot of a dense terminal-UI (TUI) dashboard filling the whole frame,
    the "Learning Plan Dashboard" of a terminal knowledge-base tool — a goal-tracking mission-control
    view. Cool dark blue-graphite background; crisp box-drawn panes packed edge to edge; monospaced
    text; block-glyph meter bars and sparklines; NOT a web page.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (top plan header + 2x2 pane grid + bottom footer):
    - TOP PLAN HEADER STRIP: plan goal title "Plan · AWS ML Certification", a "WEEK 4 / 12" marker, and
      one wide horizontal progress meter drawn as a block bar (part filled, part hollow) with a
      right-aligned "38%" in mono. An active tab among "[plan] [milestones] [stats] [log]" carries a
      magenta underline.
    - TOP-LEFT PANE "MILESTONES" (the ACTIVE pane — electric-magenta border, one-step-lighter fill): a
      checklist of plan milestones, each row a status glyph + label + tiny date — done rows a green ✓,
      the current row a magenta ▸ with a highlighted band and a magenta left-edge bar, pending rows a
      dim ○. ~7 rows.
    - TOP-RIGHT PANE "WEEKLY STATS": three or four compact stat readouts as key:value mono lines with a
      block sparkline each — "cards reviewed  142  ▂▃▅▆▇", "quiz accuracy  86%  ▄▅▄▆▇", "retention
      74%", "streak 9d" — small labels in grotesk, big numbers in mono.
    - BOTTOM-LEFT PANE "EXPERTISE": domain expertise levels as small bracketed level badges with tiny
      meter bars — "transformers  L3 ███░", "optimization  L2 ██░░", "systems  L1 █░░░" — the plan is
      calibrated against these.
    - BOTTOM-RIGHT PANE "SESSION LOG": a recent-activity feed, compact mono rows with relative
      timestamps and a leading action glyph (e.g. "2h  ✓ quiz passed · optimization", "5h  ⟳ 20 cards
      due", "1d  ＋ article added"). This pane is inactive (dim graphite border).
    - BOTTOM KEYBIND FOOTER: a persistent dim row —
      "[j/k]move  [space]toggle  [tab]pane  [n]new-plan  :cmd  ?help".

    PALETTE & TYPE: cool blue-graphite neutrals everywhere (never warm gray), cool off-white ink for
    data; the ONLY saturated hue on chrome is the electric magenta on the active-pane border, the
    current-milestone bar, and the active tab. Meter fills and status use signal green / amber / blue,
    each reinforced by a glyph — never color alone. Monospaced tabular figures align every number and
    bar; pane titles and labels are a tight grotesk small-caps.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: crisp rectangles, radius 0-1px, no rounded cards, no pills, no drop shadows;
    depth is box-drawing rules plus the one-step-lighter active tone only. Titled panes carry their
    label inline in the top rule.

    MOOD: a professional instrument panel for a learning goal — many live gauges, one signal color,
    everything measured and current; dense, cool, awake.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, browser window chrome, rounded cards, drop shadows, marketing hero whitespace, pastel gradient dashboard cards, blurry, distorted UI"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches the screen: plan header with overall progress meter, a milestone tracker with check-off states, weekly stat readouts, expertise level badges, a session-log feed"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Cool graphite TUI with box-drawing panes, single magenta signal, block-glyph meters/sparklines, four-color status with glyphs, mono data + grotesk labels, radius 0-1, no shadows"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Dense packed pane-grid terminal dashboard with clear hierarchy, plausible real TUI; persistent keybind footer"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9, terminal window (no browser chrome), no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "rendered as a web page / browser or as big rounded pastel dashboard cards instead of a dense terminal"

tags: [cockpit, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup]
